``

Order: DEFAULT_TRACKER env FIRST, then tracker.provider(), then 'jira'. Hmm — the PR description says "Updated writeSolutionAndLabels.detectTrackerType to consult tracker.provider() first." — but the code consults DEFAULT_TRACKER env first! Description inaccuracy. More importantly: precedence inconsistency — `trackers._rawProviderCandidate` order is customParams.trackerProvider → config.tracker.provider → DEFAULT_TRACKER env → config.defaultTracker; `configLoader.resolveTrackerType` order is DEFAULT_TRACKER env → config.tracker.provider → config.defaultTracker (trackerOverride wins overall); `writeSolutionAndLabels.detectTrackerType` is DEFAULT_TRACKER env → tracker.provider() → 'jira'. Three different precedence orders across three modules. The tracker.js probe order (the canonical factory) puts config.tracker.provider ABOVE DEFAULT_TRACKER env. configLoader.resolveTrackerType puts env ABOVE config. That means: a deployment with DEFAULT_TRACKER=jira env (deployment-level) and project config tracker.provider=ado → createTracker builds an ADO tracker, but `resolveTrackerType` (cliPromptsByTracker selection) picks jira prompts, and detectTrackerType picks jira markup routing in writeSolutionAndLabels. Inconsistent — the same run could build an ADO tracker while formatting output as Jira markup.

Hmm wait — is that reachable? DEFAULT_TRACKER env is described as "the deployment-level signal; it reflects which tracker integration is actually active in the Java runtime". If the Java runtime has jira active (DEFAULT_TRACKER=jira) but the project config says ado... which should win? The trackers.js header comment says the probe order has config.tracker.provider (step 2) BEFORE DEFAULT_TRACKER env (step 3) — meaning project config is more specific and wins. But configLoader.resolveTrackerType (used for choosing prompt files) was just changed to prefer... wait, what was it BEFORE this PR?

Before:
```js
function resolveTrackerType(config, options) {
 var trackerType = null;
 try { trackerType = java.lang.System.getenv('DEFAULT_TRACKER'); } catch (e) {}
 if (!trackerType && config.defaultTracker) { trackerType = config.defaultTracker; }
 if (!trackerType) { trackerType = 'jira'; }
 if (options && options.trackerOverride) { trackerType = options.trackerOverride; }
