``
 *  3. DEFAULT_TRACKER env var       — the deployment-level signal; it
 *     reflects which tracker integration is actually active in the Java
 *     runtime (jira_* / ado_* / github_* tools). This is what lets the
 *     same script run unchanged on GitHub-tracker deployments whose
 *     project config never mentions a tracker.
``

So order 2 (config.tracker.provider) before 3 (env) is pre-existing in trackers.js and NOT changed by this PR. The PR only changed configLoader.resolveTrackerType (env → config.tracker.provider → config.defaultTracker) and writeSolutionAndLabels.detectTrackerType (env → tracker.provider()). Since both now implement env-first, they're consistent with EACH OTHER and with the PRE-EXISTING resolveTrackerType order (env → defaultTracker → jira). The only inconsistent one is trackers.js createTracker's pre-existing config-first order — out of scope. So: not a new problem introduced; a pre-existing cross-module precedence divergence that the PR now makes more visible (project config now consulted in more places, each with different precedence). I'll file a SUGESTION about documenting/aligning precedence, noting it's pre-existing.

